As of Sunday, the toll from the flash floods in the Himalayan nation stood at 1,450, with 6,000 people still missing, the Indian news agency PTI reported, quoting the Nepalese police.

Mr Wagle was in India for a three-day visit during which he met finance minister Nirmala Sitharaman to discuss bilateral economic ties as well as the neighbour’s commitment to support disaster recovery and rehabilitation efforts.

He also met Indian foreign minister S Jaishankar to “reset” diplomatic ties, according to the Hindu.

open image in gallery {"id":"trigger-autogallery-42452","index":0} Aftermath of the flash floods in Trishuli, Nuwakot district, Nepal ( Reuters )

Last week, Nepali authorities said only about seven per cent of the bodies recovered since the floods had been identified.

