In spite of all that, only 105 bodies had been identified and handed to family members thus far.

Thermal drones and helicopters had been deployed to search for the missing and specialists had been brought in to help rescue hydropower project workers trapped inside tunnels.

open image in gallery {"id":"trigger-autogallery-42453","index":1} Nepalese soldiers carry the bodies of workers recovered during a search and rescue operation at the Chilime hydropower project following flash floods in Rasuwa ( AP )

Efforts to locate people still missing had also resulted in several remarkable rescues from tunnels at hydropower projects across Nepal, authorities said.

However, families of foreign nationals said updates on rescue operations, which had previously been issued regularly, had become less frequent.

